sp_configure.examples.reconfigure-trap.sql:
-- This only demonstrates the read side; it doesn't actually send a change (server-level, affects the whole instance):
-- EXEC sp_configure N'show advanced options', 1; RECONFIGURE;
-- Passing a second value to sp_configure only "queues" the change: config_value changes right away, run_value stays old --
-- RECONFIGURE is what makes run_value catch up; forgetting it is the classic "why didn't my change take effect"
EXEC sp_configure N'show advanced options';
-- Result: check the run_value column for what's actually in effect, not config_value
